  "measurement_plan": "§9 of the report — seven pre-conditions the r40 leg must satisfy to be decidable: (1) freeze the class->trigger list to a lane file before any candidate bytes exist and record its digest; (2) widen classify() to all 10 reachable classes and read the class from the tool's anchored 'REFUSAL <CLASS>:' banner (verified fix, §7); (3) widen the probe set to at minimum RECORD-EMPTY and RECORD-OUTSIDE-ROOT, plus the five wrapped-only classes if the join is to be exercised; (4) require an observed class with no docstring entry to be a FAIL, never a skip (kills the F4 mutant); (5) require each trigger string to be unique to its class (kills the '--root' collision); (6) state the join rule and the absence rule; (7) report the joined analyzer's verdict on the real base bytes as well as on a synthetic probe (the base already carries five wrapped-only triggers, so a synthetic probe is not needed).",
